WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.760
Okay, so maybe 2020 wasn't the greatest year&nbsp;
for Hollywood blockbusters — but the good news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.000
is the future's looking bright. From&nbsp;
firm franchise favorites to the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.080
exciting new projects, here are the&nbsp;
must-watch movies of the next few years.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.680
Thanks to the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;
in 2020 Marvel Studios had their first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.640
year without a theatrical release in a&nbsp;
very, very long time. That's okay, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.360
because 2021 promises to be an especially&nbsp;
robust year for Marvel's superheroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.880
and it all kicks off in May with&nbsp;
the long-awaited Black Widow.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.200
Since her character didn't survive the events&nbsp;
of Avengers: Endgame, Natasha Romanoff's solo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.880
adventure will take her back in time,&nbsp;
to the period between Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.120
Civil War and Avengers: Infinity War.&nbsp;
After the breakup of the Avengers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.360
Black Widow is called back home to untangle&nbsp;
a conspiracy with roots in her own past.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.760
Though she's venturing out on this adventure&nbsp;
without any of her fellow Avengers, Natasha will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.320
be joined by a team of some of her old Russian&nbsp;
friends, including her sister-in-arms Yelena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.760
her mentor Melina, and the former Russian super&nbsp;
soldier known as the Red Guardian. Originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.840
slated to arrive in May 2020, Black Widow will&nbsp;
now roll out a year later, on May 7th, 2021.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.880
After years of rumors suggesting that his&nbsp;
time as James Bond would be coming to a close,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.640
it's now been confirmed that the 25th James&nbsp;
Bond film, No Time to Die, will mark the curtain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.440
call for Daniel Craig. Though he's made fewer&nbsp;
films than previous title-holder Roger Moore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.160
Craig has now been the reigning Bond for a&nbsp;
longer period of time than any other actor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.560
By the time No Time to Die hits theaters, he'll&nbsp;
have spent a decade and a half in the role.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.160
“The name's Bond. James Bond."

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.600
It's fitting, then, that he seems to be&nbsp;
going out with a very big bang indeed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.400
Director Cary Fukunaga helms&nbsp;
the latest Bond adventure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:52.160
which sees Craig's 007 facing off against the&nbsp;
sinister new villain known as Safin. No Time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:57.600
to Die was originally set for a November 2020&nbsp;
release, but was pushed back a number of times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.680
due to the COVID-19 pandemic. It's&nbsp;
now slated for an April 2021 release.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.520
There have been two films in&nbsp;
the Kingsman series so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.880
and they've both focused on largely&nbsp;
the same cast of characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.840
But that's set to change in 2021, when the&nbsp;
franchise goes back to where it all began.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.880
The King's Man, a prequel film once again helmed&nbsp;
by original Kingsman director Matthew Vaughn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.280
will venture back to the early 20th century,&nbsp;
finding a different set of Kingsman agents as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.000
they try to stop a team of criminal masterminds&nbsp;
from wiping out millions of lives. Since the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.320
movie is set a hundred years ago, you probably&nbsp;
shouldn't expect to see Eggsy or Harry show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.280
up — but the cast, led by Ralph Fiennes and&nbsp;
Gemma Arterton, is pretty dazzling nonetheless.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:43.520
The film was originally set to arrive in November&nbsp;
2019, then was pushed to February 2020, and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:49.040
again to September 2020. Things took a turn for&nbsp;
the worse when the COVID-19 pandemic hit, forcing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.960
another schedule shift. The film is now set to&nbsp;
finally hit theaters on February 12th, 2021.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.520
Frank Herbert's hugely influential sci-fi novel&nbsp;
Dune has already been adapted to the screen twice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:07.040
— once for the big screen by David Lynch and once&nbsp;
for the small in a Syfy miniseries. Both versions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:13.680
have their fans, but 2020 was supposed to bring&nbsp;
a Dune adaptation like no other: a big-budget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:20.320
ultra-ambitious epic helmed by genre luminary&nbsp;
and Blade Runner 2049 director Denis Villeneuve.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:25.040
Sadly, the COVID-19 pandemic means Dune fans&nbsp;
will have to wait a little longer to see whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:30.000
Villeneuve has pulled it off or not, but that&nbsp;
doesn't make it any less exciting. The first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.600
trailer for Dune was packed full of astonishing&nbsp;
visuals, setting a truly beautiful stage for this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.880
story of a doomed family and the hostile planet&nbsp;
they make their home. Dune was originally set to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.600
be released during the 2020 holiday season, but&nbsp;
ongoing pandemic concerns meant that the release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:52.000
date has shifted. The movie will now arrive in&nbsp;
theaters and on HBO Max on October 1st, 2021.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:59.040
It's been more than 20 years since the last film&nbsp;
in the Candyman series, but in 2021 that's set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:04.480
to change — with director Nia DaCosta's sequel&nbsp;
to the original urban legend-driven classic.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.600
Set long after the first movie's creepy housing&nbsp;
projects have been torn down, the film follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.080
visual artist Anthony as he moves into the&nbsp;
now-gentrified complex with his girlfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:19.520
and begins an art project digging into the local&nbsp;
folklore. What begins as an intriguing idea soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:25.280
turns into a nightmare, however, as he discovers&nbsp;
the legend of the Candyman is frighteningly real.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.400
Candyman was originally set&nbsp;
to be released in June 2020.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.760
Pandemic-induced delays pushed it to&nbsp;
the fall of the same year, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:37.600
and then delayed the movie again to its&nbsp;
current release date of August 27th, 2021

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:43.920
On July 9th, 2021, Marvel will release&nbsp;
Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:49.200
a superhero epic with a kung fu edge.&nbsp;
Chinese-Canadian actor Simu Liu has landed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.400
the title role of Marvel's Master of Kung Fu&nbsp;
in the film, which will also star Awkwafina in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.600
an as-yet-undisclosed role. But aside from&nbsp;
being Marvel's first Asian-led MCU movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.200
perhaps the most exciting thing&nbsp;
about Shang-Chi is the villain.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:08.560
2010's Iron Man 3 seemed to introduce the&nbsp;
classic comic villain known as the Mandarin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.920
only to then reveal he was simply an actor playing&nbsp;
a role as part of another villain's evil ploy.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.720
"It's just a role. The&nbsp;
Mandarin. See, it's not real."

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:23.440
But the MCU later hinted that the real&nbsp;
Mandarin is still out there — and now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:29.600
it seems, his time has come. The genuine&nbsp;
Mandarin will make his MCU debut in Shang-Chi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.560
as played by the legendary&nbsp;
Hong Kong actor Tony Leung.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:39.200
Every once in a while, Disney will take a couple&nbsp;
of bankable stars, throw a bunch of money at them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.320
and send them on a crazy, standalone&nbsp;
adventure. And sometimes it even works out.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.800
Based on the Disney theme park ride of the&nbsp;
same name, Jungle Cruise pairs Dwayne "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.400
Rock" Johnson alongside Emily Blunt, as they set&nbsp;
out on an adventure into the heart of the jungle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.800
searching for the mythical Tree of Life.&nbsp;
The Commuter's Jaume Collet-Serra's takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.360
directing duties on the film, which was&nbsp;
originally set to be released on July 24th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.840
2020. For reasons that should be obvious&nbsp;
at this point, the film was delayed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.800
and is now due to hit theaters on July 30th, 2021.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:17.840
In 2018, the Halloween franchise returned to&nbsp;
the silver screen in a big way. Featuring the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:22.240
return of Jamie Lee Curtis as Laurie Strode,&nbsp;
the movie ignored every previous sequel to John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:28.640
Carpenter's 1978 original, setting the scene for a&nbsp;
showdown between Strode and Michael Myers that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:33.200
four decades in the making. But, as&nbsp;
it turns out, it wasn't their last.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.840
In July 2019, Carpenter and Curtis&nbsp;
announced that two more sequels are coming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:42.560
chronicling the continued struggles of Laurie&nbsp;
Strode and her family against the specter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.760
the Shape. Curtis will return, of course, as will&nbsp;
the previous movie's director, David Gordon Green.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.680
The two sequels were originally set to arrive&nbsp;
one year apart, in October of 2020 and '21, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:59.920
like so many other releases, they fell victim to&nbsp;
a reshuffling. The first sequel, Halloween Kills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:06.560
will now land in theaters on October 15th, 2021.&nbsp;
The second, Halloween Ends, hasn't been given a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:12.320
firm release date, having been bumped from 2021 by&nbsp;
its predecessor. Whenever it does arrive, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.000
you can expect that final movie to provide&nbsp;
a fitting end to the tale of Laurie Strode.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.760
It's been a long road already&nbsp;
for the Uncharted movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.680
and, unfortunately, it seems like&nbsp;
the road just keeps getting longer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.880
Active development on a film based on the hit game&nbsp;
series can be traced back to at least 2010, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.680
over the course of a decade the project has seen&nbsp;
a number of writers and directors come and go.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.120
The movie finally landed on Venom's&nbsp;
Ruben Fleischer as director,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.360
and will star Tom Holland as a younger&nbsp;
version of the video game series' hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.680
Nathan Drake. Uncharted is set to explore&nbsp;
Drake's early days as a treasure hunter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.600
and will co-star Mark Wahlberg as the young&nbsp;
adventuerer's partner, Victor Sullivan.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:55.120
In January 2020, Deadline reported&nbsp;
that Sony Pictures had bumped the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.200
film from its previous release date&nbsp;
of December 18th, 2020 to March 5th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:04.720
2021. There was still one more delay in&nbsp;
store, however, when industry reshuffling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.840
in the wake of the coronavirus pandemic&nbsp;
saw Uncharted pushed to July 16th, 2021.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:16.560
In 2018, MGM decided it was time to bring the&nbsp;
beloved video game franchise Tomb Raider back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:21.200
to the big screen — with a new take that hewed&nbsp;
closer to the more recent installments of the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:26.320
series. Starring Alicia Vikander as Lara Croft,&nbsp;
the film dove into Croft's first treasure hunt as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:32.400
she followed in the footsteps of her father.&nbsp;
Tomb Raider grossed $275 million worldwide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.840
which proved more than enough to set&nbsp;
development of a sequel in motion.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.800
Vikander will return to her&nbsp;
starring role as Lara Croft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.040
and cult genre director Ben Wheatley will sit&nbsp;
in the director's chair. The screenplay has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.360
been written by Wheatley's longtime partner Amy&nbsp;
Jump, who co-wrote the director's other films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:52.640
including High Rise and Free Fire. Tomb Raider&nbsp;
2 was first slated for release on March 19th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:57.680
2021, but has now been delayed&nbsp;
indefinitely as a result of the pandemic.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.080
For more than a decade, Dwayne&nbsp;
Johnson has been pushing for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:06.720
development of a superhero movie that sits&nbsp;
particularly close to his heart. And soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.840
he'll finally make his big-screen super-debut.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:13.200
Starring in the movie of the same&nbsp;
name, Johnson will play Black Adam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.120
a character first introduced as a villain&nbsp;
for the superhero now known as Shazam.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:22.320
Adam had previously wielded Shazam's powers,&nbsp;
but was corrupted into villainy — before long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.080
however, the character was later&nbsp;
retconned to be more of an antihero.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:31.040
Adam was originally supposed to be a villain in&nbsp;
the first Shazam! movie, but Johnson's commitment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:36.480
to the role and his view of Adam as a heroic,&nbsp;
misunderstood figure won out, and the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.960
will now be getting his very own movie. Black&nbsp;
Adam is currently awaiting a new release date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:45.680
after being bumped from its originally&nbsp;
scheduled release of December 22nd, 2021.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.600
"All of you around the world right now watching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:53.920
I can promise you this. I give you my word. We&nbsp;
are gonna go beyond your wildest expectations."

00:09:54.720 --> 00:10:00.880
In late 2018 and early 2019, Warner Bros. did a&nbsp;
lot of work to try and inject some fun into the DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:06.000
Extended Universe. That effort began with&nbsp;
Aquaman, which was a massive box office hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:11.840
over the 2018 holiday season, and continued with&nbsp;
Shazam!, which arrived in early 2019 and proved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.640
equally successful with fans and critics.&nbsp;
The movie never quite reached the box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:22.080
office heights of Aquaman, but it still&nbsp;
hauled in a decent $366 million worldwide.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.920
Then, in late 2019, Warner Bros. announced&nbsp;
that a Shazam! sequel is on the way. Zachary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.840
Levi is set to return in the film's title&nbsp;
role, with director David F. Sandberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.400
also set to return behind the camera. In&nbsp;
2020, the title was revealed to be Shazam!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:41.680
Fury of the Gods. There's no word yet on exactly&nbsp;
what the plot will be, but the original film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:46.400
set up plenty of opportunities for new foes,&nbsp;
including the potential introduction of Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:52.480
Adam after his own film drops. Fury of the Gods&nbsp;
is currently expected to arrive on June 2nd, 2023.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:59.520
Ask any long-time Star Wars fan what kind of&nbsp;
movie they'd like to see outside the main saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:03.440
and there's a good chance you'll hear the&nbsp;
words "Rogue Squadron." The legendary band&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.520
of starfighter pilots was a major part&nbsp;
of the old Star Wars Expanded Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.680
and now it seems set to be part of the new one.

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:14.640
Disney announced in December 2020 that Wonder&nbsp;
Woman director Patty Jenkins will helm a Rogue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:19.440
Squadron feature film, and that it will be the&nbsp;
next theatrical release in the Star Wars universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:23.120
In a short video introducing the&nbsp;
project, Jenkins described the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:27.440
as the fulfillment of a lifelong dream&nbsp;
to make an amazing fighter pilot movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:30.240
in honor of her father, who&nbsp;
was a fighter pilot himself.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.440
"Now I've found a movie about two things&nbsp;
I love. So I'm gonna see you very soon."

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:40.240
Plot details are scarce, but we do&nbsp;
know that the film will focus on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:46.160
"a new generation" of pilots in a "future era"&nbsp;
of the Star Wars galaxy. More will become clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:50.640
in the run-up to Rogue Squadron's release,&nbsp;
which has been slated for December 2023.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:56.640
Acclaimed writer/director Taika Waititi already&nbsp;
has something of a history with Star Wars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:01.520
After finding considerable success at Marvel&nbsp;
Studios with Thor: Ragnarok, Waititi joined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:06.400
the group of directors recruited by Jon Favreau to&nbsp;
helm the first season of the Star Wars live-action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.760
series The Mandalorian, in which he also voiced&nbsp;
the bounty hunter turned nanny droid IG-11.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.840
Waititi must have made an impression&nbsp;
on the Lucasfilm crew, because in May&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:20.800
2020 the official Star Wars website announced&nbsp;
that the director has signed on to make a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:25.440
Star Wars movie. Details on the project&nbsp;
are still extremely scarce, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:29.200
and nobody has any idea what it'll&nbsp;
be called, when it'll be set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:33.360
which characters are involved, or even when&nbsp;
it's supposed to be released. All anyone can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:39.280
be sure of is that Waititi is working on a Star&nbsp;
Wars movie. But hey, that's good enough for now.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:45.760
The earliest rumblings around Disney's purchase&nbsp;
of Fox immediately sent waves of anticipation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:50.560
through the Marvel fandom. By the time the deal&nbsp;
was done, geeks everywhere were champing at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:56.080
bit for any news about the future of Fox's&nbsp;
two biggest Marvel properties: the X-Men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.080 --> 00:13:01.840
and the Fantastic Four. Mostly, however, Kevin&nbsp;
Feige and company kept a tight lid on things.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:06.880
Then came Disney's Investor Day presentation&nbsp;
in December 2020, when Feige announced that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:11.440
Fantastic Four movie is on the horizon.&nbsp;
Very little is known about the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.360
but it has been announced that Spider-Man&nbsp;
director Jon Watts will be at the helm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.520
Aside from that? Anything could happen.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:22.720
Though they first felt more like a relatively&nbsp;
minor part of the wider MCU narrative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.080
the Ant-Man movies have since become a&nbsp;
kind of cornerstone for the future of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:30.880
the franchise — mostly thanks to Scott Lang's&nbsp;
major role in Avengers: Endgame. Now, the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:36.000
adventure for the Ant-Man crew is on the horizon,&nbsp;
and, ironically enough, it's set to be a big one.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.360
Marvel announced in December 2020 that&nbsp;
the third feature in the series will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:43.440
titled Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania,&nbsp;
and that it's set to introduce one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:48.720
biggest villains in the Marvel Universe:&nbsp;
the time-hopping warlord Kang the Conqueror.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.160
Lovecraft Country star Jonathan&nbsp;
Majors is set to portray Kang,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:58.160
making him one of two major MCU newcomers in&nbsp;
the film so far, the other being Freaky star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:03.040
Kathryn Newton as Scott Lang's grown-up daughter&nbsp;
Cassie. Ant-Man and the Wasp stars Paul Rudd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:07.280
Evangeline Lilly, Michael Douglas, and Michelle&nbsp;
Pfeiffer are all set to return for the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:11.040
as is director Peyton Reed. The film&nbsp;
does not yet have a firm release date.

00:14:12.885 --> 00:14:16.000
Captain Marvel was a game-changer&nbsp;
for the MCU when it debuted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.480
in 2019. It was the first female-led&nbsp;
Marvel Studios superhero film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:24.080
it introduced the Skrulls to the franchise&nbsp;
while expanding the role of the Kree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:29.760
and it set the stage for more superheroines to&nbsp;
join the MCU. So Captain Marvel 2 was always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:34.640
going to be a big deal, and now we're starting&nbsp;
to get a sense of just how important it will be.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:39.200
Nia DaCosta is set to direct the second solo&nbsp;
adventure for the title character, but this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:44.720
Carol Danvers won't be fighting alone. She'll&nbsp;
be joined by Teyonah Parris as Monica Rambeau,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:49.040
a grown-up version of the character who debuted&nbsp;
in the first movie, and who in the comics is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:53.840
currently known as Spectrum. Joining the two&nbsp;
of them will be Iman Vellani as Kamala Khan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:59.360
a.k.a. Ms. Marvel, a Captain Marvel&nbsp;
superfan-turned-superhero who's about to debut in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:05.800
her own original series on Disney+. Captain Marvel&nbsp;
2 is set to hit theaters on November 11th, 2022.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:11.440
Not too long ago, it seemed unthinkable that&nbsp;
there'd be any more instalments in the Toy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:16.960
Story series. Then Toy Story 4 came along and&nbsp;
wrapped an even tighter bow on the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:22.000
Now, it looks like Toy Story is moving on — in&nbsp;
a way that nobody could possibly have predicted.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:27.280
In December 2020, Disney announced that Pixar&nbsp;
Animation Studios has been hard at work on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:32.080
Lightyear, a new animated adventure starring&nbsp;
Chris Evans as the voice of the title character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.160
presenting a kind of origin story&nbsp;
for everyone's favorite Space Ranger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:40.560
But as Evans later clarified via Twitter,&nbsp;
this isn't the story of the toy. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:45.600
this is the story of the "real" Buzz Lightyear&nbsp;
— the character who inspired the toy. That's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:50.880
intriguing idea, and we'll see how it plays out&nbsp;
when Lightyear hits theaters June 17th, 2022.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:56.160
Marvel Studios has been eager to produce a&nbsp;
sequel to Black Panther ever since the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.160 --> 00:16:01.600
film rocketed to massive commercial and&nbsp;
critical success in 2018. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:05.680
in 2020, Hollywood was rocked by the&nbsp;
tragic passing of Chadwick Boseman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:09.440
Boseman's death left a number of lingering&nbsp;
questions from Black Panther fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:13.200
and in December 2020, Marvel&nbsp;
started answering a few of them.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:17.680
During Disney's Investor Day presentation, Kevin&nbsp;
Feige announced that Black Panther 2 would still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:22.720
be moving forward under the leadership of director&nbsp;
Ryan Coogler, but that the role of T'Challa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:28.720
won't be recast. Instead, Feige told fans to&nbsp;
expect a movie that both honors Boseman's memory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:32.560
and continues to explore the world&nbsp;
of Wakanda. However it takes shape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:35.840
Black Panther 2 is set to&nbsp;
hit theaters July 8th, 2022.

